  planner_response {
    response: "I have built **Lalameow Rider**, an original, tactile, 3D miniature city delivery-rider game:\n\n- **Original Visual Identity & Branding**: Designed with a warm honey yellow, dusty rose, and teal palette, custom adaptive launcher icons, and a living miniature city with pastel architecture, shop awnings, illuminated storefronts, streetlamps, bridges, and weather atmospheres (Sunny Breeze, Golden Sunset, Rainy Shower, and Cozy Neon Night).\n- **Expressive 3D Cat Rider & Scooter Engine**: Custom mathematical 3D perspective projection and depth-sorted rendering system. The rider features dynamic lean-into-turn physics, steering handlebar animations, twitching 3D ears, responsive blinking eyes, waving tail physics, rotating wheels, cast shadow, and an active headlight beam.\n- **Living Miniature City**: Features 5 distinct districts (*Downpaws Market*, *Fishbone Harbor*, *Whisker Woods*, *Sunny Mew Suburbs*, and *Neon Alley*), looping NPC animal cars and mopeds, hopping pedestrians, and interactive Shell-Paws & Meow-bil gas stations.\n- **Core Delivery Mechanics**: Offers diverse job categories including steaming food bowls, express parcels, fresh market catches, catnip curios, and *The Daily Purr* newspaper runs. Includes 3D holographic waypoint beams with expanding pulse rings, directional GPS radar breadcrumbs, customer dialogue reactions, 5-star rating feedback, and tipping bonuses.\n- **Fuel & Roadside Systems**: Realistic fuel consumption with low-fuel visual and audio alerts, interactive gas station pumps, roadside paw-sistance dispatch, and a manual scooter-pushing activity if the tank runs dry.\n- **Tactile Touch Controls & Procedural Audio**: Dual-thumb control scheme with a virtual analog steering joystick, responsive Gas, Brake/Reverse, and Drift pedals, a \"MEEP!\" horn button, and a procedural synthesizer providing 2-stroke engine hum, notification chimes, delivery victory fanfares, and haptic pulses.\n- **In-Game MeowPhone & Garage Boutique**: A functional in-game smartphone with chat notifications, active delivery manifests, a PawPay wallet, and daily bounty quests. The Meow Garage provides extensive cat rider customization (name, fur coat patterns, helmets, jackets, delivery backpacks, scooter models, pastel paint jobs, and performance tier upgrades)."
    modified_response: "I have built **Lalameow Rider**, an original, tactile, 3D miniature city delivery-rider game:\n\n- **Original Visual Identity & Branding**: Designed with a warm honey yellow, dusty rose, and teal palette, custom adaptive launcher icons, and a living miniature city with pastel architecture, shop awnings, illuminated storefronts, streetlamps, bridges, and weather atmospheres (Sunny Breeze, Golden Sunset, Rainy Shower, and Cozy Neon Night).\n- **Expressive 3D Cat Rider & Scooter Engine**: Custom mathematical 3D perspective projection and depth-sorted rendering system. The rider features dynamic lean-into-turn physics, steering handlebar animations, twitching 3D ears, responsive blinking eyes, waving tail physics, rotating wheels, cast shadow, and an active headlight beam.\n- **Living Miniature City**: Features 5 distinct districts (*Downpaws Market*, *Fishbone Harbor*, *Whisker Woods*, *Sunny Mew Suburbs*, and *Neon Alley*), looping NPC animal cars and mopeds, hopping pedestrians, and interactive Shell-Paws & Meow-bil gas stations.\n- **Core Delivery Mechanics**: Offers diverse job categories including steaming food bowls, express parcels, fresh market catches, catnip curios, and *The Daily Purr* newspaper runs. Includes 3D holographic waypoint beams with expanding pulse rings, directional GPS radar breadcrumbs, customer dialogue reactions, 5-star rating feedback, and tipping bonuses.\n- **Fuel & Roadside Systems**: Realistic fuel consumption with low-fuel visual and audio alerts, interactive gas station pumps, roadside paw-sistance dispatch, and a manual scooter-pushing activity if the tank runs dry.\n- **Tactile Touch Controls & Procedural Audio**: Dual-thumb control scheme with a virtual analog steering joystick, responsive Gas, Brake/Reverse, and Drift pedals, a \"MEEP!\" horn button, and a procedural synthesizer providing 2-stroke engine hum, notification chimes, delivery victory fanfares, and haptic pulses.\n- **In-Game MeowPhone & Garage Boutique**: A functional in-game smartphone with chat notifications, active delivery manifests, a PawPay wallet, and daily bounty quests. The Meow Garage provides extensive cat rider customization (name, fur coat patterns, helmets, jackets, delivery backpacks, scooter models, pastel paint jobs, and performance tier upgrades)."
