    thinking: "**Analyzing Scale Calculation**\n\nI\'ve been examining the scale calculation in `CatRiderRenderer3D.kt`, specifically line 68. With a `depth` of 7.6f and `screenH` of 1920f, the initial calculation results in a scale of 189.4f, which is then clamped to the maximum value of 180f.\n\n\n**Revising Scale for Visibility**\n\nI\'m now focusing on ensuring the player character\'s prominence. With the current scaling, the cat appears quite small, just 162 pixels wide. This is inadequate for a mobile-first 3D game. I need to calibrate the scale to ensure the cat is vibrant and clearly visible, aiming for a width closer to 350-500 pixels. The user\'s preferences for a premium experience, player customization, and clear visibility are shaping this revision.\n\n\n**Planning Game State Flow**\n\nI\'m now outlining the game\'s initial flow. Currently, the player is thrown directly into the city, skipping character creation and tutorial steps. I\'m focusing on crafting a smoother onboarding experience. I\'m prioritizing steps like naming the cat, selecting a scooter, and a guided delivery tutorial to address projection clipping issues.\n\n\n**Designing Onboarding Experience**\n\nI\'m now fully immersed in the onboarding process, aiming for a player-friendly first impression. The new flow begins with a \"Rider & Scooter Creator Screen,\" accessible on first launch or via a Profile button. It\'ll feature a rotating 3D preview of the cat on a scooter. I\'m excited about the customization options: name, breed, expressions, accessories, and scooter selection. Following this, the first delivery quest will be a high-priority tutorial with glowing waypoints and breadcrumbs. It focuses on the player delivering an order to Madame Fluff from Neko Sushi. I\'m implementing a pulsing \"Pick Up Order\" button.\n\n\n**Defining Delivery Quest Flow**\n\nI\'m now detailing the delivery quest structure. The player selects a job from the MeowPhone, which instantly triggers an interactive loop. The order loads, the camera snaps to the pickup location, the player collects the package, and the GPS guides them to Madame Fluff\'s townhouse! Completion involves a tap to deliver and a delightful animation with rewards and an achievement badge. This leads smoothly into continuous jobs from the marketplace.\n\n\n"
