    thinking: "**Analyzing Screen Composition**\n\nOkay, I\'ve zoned in on the `CharacterCreatorScreen` composable. It\'s a full-screen element, as indicated by `Modifier.fillMaxSize()`. That \"isCharacterCreatorOpen\" flag triggered its appearance. I\'m focusing on the implications of a full-screen UI and how that impacts the broader app flow.\n\n\n**Exploring App\'s Visuals**\n\nI\'m now diving deep into the visual impact of the `CharacterCreatorScreen` blocking the `GameWorldCanvas`. My key interest is what the user *first* sees, or doesn\'t see. Initially, the user sees nothing of the intended 3D world, which has a distinct impact. This led me to inspect `CityWorld.kt` and `CityRenderer3D.kt`, to learn how buildings are positioned and rendered. I\'ve realized, the buildings were so far off to the sides that the user sees nothing.\n\n\n**Generating World Content**\n\nI\'m now focused on asset generation and placement. No parcels, newspapers, or characters were previously rendered in 3D. The game world needs all of those elements from the reference image, *including* the playable character, Nami, and her scooter, rendered from the start. I\'m prioritizing the playable character, and have realized the game will need custom 3D models and icons.\n\n\n**Constructing Scene Geometry**\n\nOkay, I\'ve defined building layouts. I\'m visualizing the town, street by street, by parsing `z` coordinates for layout. I\'m focusing on the 3D geometry of the shops, the textured facades, the awnings, the recessed doors, and the shop windows with warm glowing interiors. The goal is crafting realistic 3D models with depth. Now, I\'m thinking of building trims and roof details.\n\n\n"
