  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing the 3D Renderer**\n\nI\'ve been examining `CatRiderRenderer3D.kt` and noticed a critical issue. The cat rendering is exclusively from the back, with no face, eyes, or front details. Even though the character rotates in `CharacterCreatorScreen`, `renderCatRider` consistently draws the rear view.\n\n\n**Addressing the Character\'s Visibility**\n\nI\'ve determined the character always renders from the rear, regardless of camera angle or rotation. The issue appears in `renderCatRider`. Further investigation, prompted by user feedback on asset generation, reveals a bigger issue: the game doesn\'t launch into a playable state! I need to ensure the game boots directly into landscape with the player immediately on the scooter, as I make adjustments. I\'m focusing on `MainActivity.kt` and `AndroidManifest.xml` to lock the orientation.\n\n\n**Verifying the Landscape HUD**\n\nI\'m now implementing the HUD elements and checking they are visible in landscape mode at the start. The game should present screen controls such as virtual steering, gas and brake, and other gauges on boot. I want to see these elements, as well as a customer dialogue, active job HUD, and other elements.\n\n**Examining Building Visibility**\n\nI\'ve moved on to understanding why the 3D buildings are not visible or are clipped. I\'ve found a clue in `CityRenderer3D.kt`, which applies camera-space calculations. I\'ve reviewed the building positions in `CityWorldData.buildings` and cross referenced them with the player\'s starting position at (0,0). Given the building offsets and camera setup, I understand why the buildings were obscured. I\'m focusing on the camera\'s Z clipping distance to resolve this.\n\n\n**Calculating Building Dimensions**\n\nI\'m now calculating building dimensions in camera space and projecting them onto the screen. I\'m focusing on the `BuildingRenderable.draw()` function, particularly the camera-space corner calculations. I\'m carefully examining the building\'s width and length relative to the camera\'s position and the `projectCameraPoint` calls. I believe I have the logic, I need to debug the code.\n\n\n**Correcting Building Rendering**\n\nI\'ve been meticulously examining the building rendering logic, and I\'ve pinpointed a critical flaw. The `draw()` function in `BuildingRenderable` had an incorrect wall rendering setup. Notably, the code was drawing the far north and east walls, while completely omitting the south and west walls. This explains why buildings appeared incomplete or obscured from certain angles. I will make sure the wall logic handles all facing and rotation for my game.\n\n\n**Determining Surface Visibility**\n\nI\'m now determining face visibility using cross-products in screen space to check signed areas. The goal is to draw the appropriate building faces. I\'m focusing on the logic to compute surface normals and the signed area of each quad face: south, north, east, west, and roof. I\'ve broken down the rendering of a 3D box into individual faces and the corresponding vertices.\n\n\n**Designing Delivery Items**\n\nI\'m now focusing on adding delivery items such as newspapers and parcels. I\'m thinking I should build a dedicated 3D item renderer, perhaps `DeliveryItemRenderer3D`, or I could integrate it with the `CityRenderer3D` and `CatRiderRenderer3D`. I am also working on adding colorful awnings, storefront signboards, and clear window panes to each building\'s visible faces. I also want to build ground curbs and pavements.\n\n\n**Creating Delivery Indicators**\n\nI\'m now designing visual cues for deliveries. I\'m imagining a holographic beacon with pulsing rings and a rotating 3D model: a cardboard parcel, rolled newspaper, or bakery box. Sparkle particles will enhance the items. A floating billboard will display customer details.\n\nI\'m also considering integrating the 3D delivery items directly onto the scooter when a job is active, as either a strapped parcel on the backpack, or side-rack bundles of newspapers.\n\n\n**Developing the Character Model**\n\nI\'m now diving into the `CatRiderRenderer3D` to give the character a proper 3D model that changes with the camera. I need the cat to have a face, front view, and scooter details. This requires adding a front view, expressive facial features, animated eyes, and the scooter\'s front components like the headlight and tire. I want Nami\'s courier jacket to match her unique front view.\n\n\n**Generating the Scooter Assets**\n\nI\'m now focused on the scooter\'s rear view, detailing the bodywork, spinning tire, taillight, delivery box, and delivery items. I want Nami\'s posture to show dynamic lean, jacket wrinkles, tail movement, a helmet, mirrors and turn signals, and dual exhaust smoke puffs. I\'m also ensuring the character\'s scale is correct for visibility. I\'ve also added the main hero rider image.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 9
      nanos: 105505708
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
