    thinking: "**Visualize Parcel Rendering**\n\nI\'ve been examining `CatRiderRenderer3D.kt` and noticed a key detail: when a player takes a job and it\'s in the \"picked up\" state, we can display the 3D parcel directly on the backpack or cargo rack. I\'m considering how best to integrate this visual cue to signify a loaded delivery. Currently, I\'m focusing on incorporating the 3D parcel based on the delivery category.\n\n\n**Refine Delivery Visualization**\n\nI\'m now thinking about specific visual representations. For newspapers, I envision rolled bundles on the luggage racks, headlines visible! Parcels will be a 3D box, secured with bungee cords and fragile tape. Food deliveries could be a steaming box or thermal container. I\'m also considering front-view camera angles. To render the front, I\'ll need to calculate camera-to-rider vectors and rider heading, rendering the front view if the dot product of these vectors is negative. This opens the door for rendering the front wheel, forks, and the yellow apron!\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 1
      nanos: 889790290
