  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Visualizing Customer Avatars**\n\nI\'m now thinking about the `CustomerInteractionDialog`. A key update: We can display the actual customer avatar! For example, if the customer is Momo, we can use `R.drawable.char_momo`. If it is Lily, we can use `R.drawable.char_lily`. Grandma Whiskers would use `R.drawable.char_grandma`, while Benny\'s avatar is yet to be determined.\n\n\n**Expanding Character Avatars**\n\nI\'ve expanded the avatar logic! Now, Mr. Pickles gets a pigeon avatar. I\'m also planning how to visualize items in `DeliveryRequestDialog` and MeowPhone, showing icons for deliveries like parcels and croissants. Also, Nami is now the primary 3D character!\nI\'m ensuring her scooter is always rendered front and center. I\'m adding 3D items to her scooter rack, a newspaper roll for paper routes, or a parcel for other jobs! I\'m also working on enhancements: a clear yellow helmet with cat ears and goggles, and a yellow courier jacket with a paw emblem.\n\n\n**Developing Nami\'s Environment**\n\nI\'m making excellent progress on Nami\'s world! I\'m adding detail to her 3D model: Her hands are holding the scooter handlebars, and the scooter now has a chrome headlight that casts a dynamic light cone. Dual chrome round mirrors are visible, too. I\'m focusing on dynamic effects: rotating wheels and a tail that sways with physics. I\'ve also incorporated a contact shadow on the asphalt.\n\n\n\n**Mapping Out Shops**\n\nI\'m now mapping out shop locations relative to the player\'s starting point, thinking about Z-axis positioning and X-axis offsets to create a balanced environment. I\'m visualizing the immediate surroundings; there\'s Lily\'s Bakery on the left and Neko Ramen on the right. Further ahead, I see Boba Whiskers Cafe, The Daily Purr Press, and Post Paws Courier Hub and Benny\'s Shell-Paws.\n\n\n**Visualizing Delivery Locations**\n\nI\'m now visualizing delivery locations in 3D. I\'m focusing on the visual cues for pickups and deliveries. Outside Post Hub and Lily\'s Bakery, I\'m imagining parcel stacks. At The Daily Purr, I see rolled newspaper stacks. I\'m rendering a pulsating gold beacon for pickups, and a teal target ring for deliveries. Within 4 meters, I plan to display contextual buttons. When tapped, the parcel will animate.\n\n\n**Rendering 3D Buildings**\n\nI\'m now implementing robust 3D building rendering in `CityRenderer3D.kt`. I\'m focusing on rendering complete building faces with awnings, windows, and signs, as opposed to the previous implementation which had many bugs! I\'ve started by implementing a visibility check for each face (front, sides, back, roof) based on camera position and building position, so I can apply backface culling. This also allows me to check if the building is on the east or west side of the street, so I can ensure the proper facades are displayed.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 5
      nanos: 219811185
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
