    thinking: "**Implementing Cat Face Feature**\n\nI\'m currently working on adding the adorable cat face feature. Specifically, I\'m focusing on rendering it when the camera views the rider from a front or 3/4 angle, conditional on `isFacingCamera` within `CatRiderRenderer3D.kt`. I\'m calculating an `angleDiff` to determine the appropriate rendering conditions.\n\n\n**Refining Face Rendering**\n\nI\'ve been refining the cat face rendering logic. I am currently concentrating on the placement and size of the muzzle patch and cheeks, adjusting offsets and radii. Additionally, I\'m working to make the eyes look more expressive, but the current algorithm is still not complete.\n\n\n**Adjusting Eye Expression**\n\nI\'m now focusing on eye rendering, particularly adapting for blinking. I am currently working on the visual characteristics of closed versus open eyes. When blinking, I am drawing curved arcs for a happier expression. The open eyes are using a layered approach, starting with a dark outer circle to give them a distinct anime style.\n\n\n**Optimizing Eye Detail**\n\nI\'m now iterating on the eye rendering details. I\'m focusing on creating more distinct anime-style eyes, using layered circles for the iris and pupil. I\'ve added catchlight sparkles to give the eyes more life. I\'ve chosen colors for the iris and pupil, and I\'m experimenting with different radii for each layer.\n\n\n**Adding Cat Smile**\n\nI\'ve moved on to drawing the cat\'s nose and smile. I\'m focusing on the position and color of the nose, using DustyRose, and I\'m currently working to position the cat smile, using drawArc with offsets. I\'m using path calculations to form the pink nose and setting color and stroke width, and I\'m adding offsets to the smile to position it correctly on the face.\n\n\n"
