  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Examining CatRiderRenderer3D.kt**\n\nI\'ve started delving into `CatRiderRenderer3D.kt` and am focused on the conditional rendering of 3D parcels. I\'m noting that a parcel is rendered on the rack if there\'s a custom carrier parcel or by default. I\'m now looking at how to adjust the rendering logic to accommodate various scenarios. The goal is to make the visuals more adaptable.\n\n\n**Analyzing Parcel Rendering**\n\nI\'ve examined the code to ensure a 3D parcel is always visible on the scooter. If a job is active and picked up, it renders the specific job item (newspaper, box, or parcel). Otherwise, it renders a default parcel. This ensures visual consistency and gives Nami\'s scooter an appealing look. I\'ll now start working on the AssetLibraryDialog.kt to display game assets.\n\n\n"
